7: ## 🛠️ Changes Implemented
8: 
9: ### 1. First-Layer Local Routing (`pkg/llm/local.go`)
10: - Added a fallback-routing mechanism in `GenerateSummary`.
11: - The worker first attempts to route text generation requests to your local **Ollama** server running at `http://127.0.0.1:11434` utilizing the customized `sovereign-oracle` model.
12: - If the Ollama server is offline or fails, the handler falls back to the secondary local gateway (e.g., LM Studio).
13: 
14: ### 2. Dual-Agent Memory Reconstruction (`pkg/rtgo` & `pkg/agent`)
15: - Added `GetAgentMemoryContext` in `Store` and `Manager` to load Swarm Cluster, Agent Role, and historical ticket logs/actions for a given agent ID.
16: - Updated the ticket worker in `pkg/agent/worker.go` to fetch memory contexts for **both** the creator agent (`t.Creator`) and the assigned agent (`t.AssignedTo`), injecting both contexts directly into the LLM prompts.
17: 
18: ### 3. Automated Subsidiary Ticket Creation & Linkage (`pkg/agent/worker.go`)
19: - Programmed a trigger mechanism that scans local LLM responses for failure patterns (keywords: `ERROR`, `FAIL`, `SELF-HEALING`, `HEAL`, `SUBSIDIARY`).
20: - On detection, it automatically generates a new subsidiary (child) ticket titled `[HEALING] Subsidiary task spawned from Ticket [ParentID]` and links it to the parent using the `CONSEQUENCE` relationship.
